  "query_preview": "..\nIssued at 229 PM CST Thu Nov 5 2026\n\nCurrently, a shortwave trough is passing over the Central Plains. \nThe associated vort max situated over the KS/OK border is leading to \nshowers and cloud cover across south-central Kansas with a few \nisolated thunderstorms in northern OK. In the wake of the broader \ntrough and cold front, temperatures today linger in the upper 50s. \nWith northerly flow and another shortwave approaching the area on \nFriday, low clouds will continue for northern and eastern portions \nof the forecast area along with the chance for some spotty drizzle. \nTemperatures on Friday will once again remain the the 50s for much \nof the forecast area. The shortwave will traverse the region on \nSaturday with clouds clearing the area from west to east throughout \nthe day. Temperatures will begin to rebound with highs in the lower \n60s for central Kansas.\n\nFor Sunday into mid-week, broad troughing will build over the \nWestern US and across the Plains. Dry weather, mostly clear \nconditions, and above normal temperatures are forecast through \nWednesday of next week. Models are hinting at another shortwave \ntowards middle/end of next week as a deep trough digs into the \nNortheast US. At this point, this feature looks to have minimal \nramifications across the forecast area and may only lead to a slight \ncool-down for the end of next week.",
